    slug: "ford-mustang-mach-e-rally-review",
    title: "Ford Mustang Mach-E Rally Review: The Slide-Happy Dirt Road Weapon",
    excerpt: "With a raised MagneRide suspension, underbody shielding, Brembo brakes, and a bespoke RallySport drive mode, Ford builds the rallycross EV we didn't know we needed.",
    body: "Most electric SUVs are designed for sterile highway cruising and urban school runs. Ford Performance took a completely different path with the Mustang Mach-E Rally: they built a dedicated, dirt-slinging rally weapon that encourages you to throw caution to the wind and slide through gravel at 60 mph.\n\nTested extensively on a custom rallycross course at Michigan Proving Grounds, the Mach-E Rally is an inspired homage to Ford's World Rally Championship heritage.\n\n![Ford Mustang Mach-E Rally in Grabber Yellow with White OZ-Style Wheels | Picture courtesy of Ford Media](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/2024_Ford_Mustang_Dark_Horse_in_Blue_Ember%2C_Front_Left%2C_08-20-2023.jpg/1280px-2024_Ford_Mustang_Dark_Horse_in_Blue_Ember%2C_Front_Left%2C_08-20-2023.jpg)\n\n## Rally Hardware Modifications\n\nFord didn't just add cosmetic stickers. The Mach-E Rally features serious mechanical upgrades:\n\n- **Suspension:** 20mm raised ride height with specially tuned MagneRide dampers and softer springs to absorb severe ruts and jumps.\n- **Underbody Protection:** Thick steel shielding protecting both front and rear electric drive units.\n- **Wheels & Tires:** 19-inch gloss-white rally wheels wrapped in bespoke Michelin CrossClimate2 all-terrain rubber with reinforced sidewalls.\n- **Powertrain:** Dual-motor AWD delivering **480 HP and 950 Nm of torque**.\n\n> \"Switch into RallySport Drive Mode, turn in aggressively, and give it full throttle. The rear electric motor snaps out, the front motor pulls the nose straight, and you exit the corner in a glorious cloud of roost.\"\n\n![Mustang Mach-E Rally Rear Wing and Off-Road Armor | Picture courtesy of Ford Performance](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/2024_Ford_Mustang_Dark_Horse_in_Blue_Ember%2C_Front_Left%2C_08-20-2023.jpg/1280px-2024_Ford_Mustang_Dark_Horse_in_Blue_Ember%2C_Front_Left%2C_08-20-2023.jpg)\n\n## Real-World Usability\n\nDespite its off-road party trick, the Mach-E Rally remains a highly practical everyday vehicle with a 91 kWh usable battery pack delivering 250 miles (402 km) of range, Ford BlueCruise hands-free highway driving, and seating for five.\n\nIt proves that electric vehicles don't have to take themselves so seriously—sometimes, the best reason to build a car is pure unadulterated fun.",
