    title: "Mercedes-AMG GT 63 S E Performance: The 805 HP V8 Hybrid Rocket",
    excerpt: "AMG pairs its handcrafted 4.0L twin-turbo V8 with an F1-derived electric motor on the rear axle to create the quickest-accelerating AMG production car in history.",
    body: "Affalterbach's mad scientists have unleashed their most potent 2-door coupe to date. The 2025 Mercedes-AMG GT 63 S E Performance combines traditional German V8 thunder with cutting-edge Formula 1 hybrid technology.\n\nPositioned on the rear axle is a 201 hp Electric Drive Unit (EDU) with an integrated 2-speed gearbox and electronically controlled limited-slip differential. Up front sits AMG's handcrafted 4.0L biturbo V8.\n\n![Mercedes-AMG GT 63 S E Performance Coupe | Picture courtesy of Mercedes-Benz Media](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Mercedes-Benz_V297_IAA_2021_1X7A0168.jpg/1280px-Mercedes-Benz_V297_IAA_2021_1X7A0168.jpg)\n\n## Devastating Hybrid Performance\n\n- **Combined Output:** 805 HP (600 kW) and 1,420 Nm of torque.\n- **0–100 km/h:** 2.8 seconds (quicker than the AMG ONE hypercar from a standstill).\n- **Top Speed:** 320 km/h (199 mph).\n- **Battery:** 6.1 kWh AMG High Performance Battery with direct cell liquid cooling designed for instant energy deployment and continuous high-rate recuperation.\n\n> \"The electric motor eliminates any hint of turbo lag. The instant you breathe on the accelerator, 1,420 Nm hits your spine like a tidal wave.\"\n\nActive roll stabilization (AMG ACTIVE RIDE CONTROL) and standard rear-axle steering ensure that this 2.1-ton luxury grand tourer corners flat and stays glued to the tarmac through high-speed sweepers.",
    category: "Review",
