    title: "1964 Aston Martin DB5: The World's Most Famous Grand Tourer",
    excerpt: "Superleggera magnesium-alloy bodywork, Connolly leather upholstery, and immortalized forever as James Bond's signature ride.",
    body: "Few cars in history are as inextricably tied to cinema and style as the 1964 Aston Martin DB5. Designed by Carrozzeria Touring in Milan using their patented *Superleggera* (superlight) magnesium-alloy tubing framework, the DB5 defined the golden age of British grand touring.\n\nWhen Sean Connery drove the Silver Birch DB5 in the 1964 film *Goldfinger*, the car became an instant cultural icon across the globe.\n\n![1964 Aston Martin DB5 Coupe in Silver Birch | Picture courtesy of Aston Martin Heritage / Wikimedia Commons](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/1964_Aston_Martin_DB5_4.0_Front.jpg/1280px-1964_Aston_Martin_DB5_4.0_Front.jpg)\n\n## British Grand Touring Perfection\n\n- **Engine:** 4.0-liter Tadek Marek all-aluminum DOHC inline-six with triple SU carburetors producing **282 HP and 288 lb-ft of torque**.\n- **Transmission:** ZF 5-speed manual gearbox.\n- **Top Speed:** 145 mph (233 km/h).\n- **Interior:** Hand-stitched Connolly leather, wool pile carpeting, and chrome Smiths instrumentation.\n\nEven without revolving license plates, ejector seats, or Browning machine guns, the DB5 is a masterpiece of proportions and elegance.",
